; Script code $95: run a subscript when a flag byte is zero
;
; Operands: subscript address (word), flag address (word). If the byte at the flag address is 0 the script at the
; subscript address is run to its $80 end by a recursive call of #R$9D5F; in either case the script goes on after the
; operands. Observed with a hand-made script and the flag byte set to 0 and to 1. The flags are bytes of the item flag
; area at $851A-$8521 (see the item table at $8EDF); used 3 times (rooms 8, 19 and 20).
;
; HL Script pointer, at the operands
; O:HL Script pointer after the operands
@label=OpRunIfZero
c$A04B CALL $A11A    ;
 $A04E LD A,(BC)     ; flag byte
 $A04F OR A          ;
 $A050 RET NZ        ;
 $A051 PUSH HL       ;
 $A052 EX DE,HL      ;
 $A053 CALL $9D5F    ; run the subscript
 $A056 POP HL        ;
 $A057 RET           ;
